Subject: [PATCH 01/15] =?UTF-8?q?3DS:=20Add=20standalone=20M=C3=A4usejagd?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20build=20mode=20(MAUSJAGD=5FPORT)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When built with -DMAUSJAGD_PORT, the 3DS port behaves like a single-game
app for "Mäusejagd im Grandhotel" (The Great Green Mouse Disaster, German):

- Started without arguments, it runs director:ggmd from
  sdmc:/3ds/mausjagd/game instead of showing the launcher
- Config, log and saves live in sdmc:/3ds/mausjagd/, so a regular
  ScummVM installation is left untouched
- The "Return to Launcher" button in the global menu is disabled

Without the define, nothing changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 backends/platform/3ds/main.cpp    | 17 +++++++++++++
 backends/platform/3ds/mausjagd.h  | 42 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 backends/platform/3ds/osystem.cpp | 15 +++++++++++
 engines/dialogs.cpp               |  4 +++
 4 files changed, 78 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 backends/platform/3ds/mausjagd.h

diff --git a/backends/platform/3ds/main.cpp b/backends/platform/3ds/main.cpp
index 159bc01eb5..10e80e951f 100644
--- a/backends/platform/3ds/main.cpp
+++ b/backends/platform/3ds/main.cpp
@@ -21,6 +21,9 @@
 
 #include "backends/platform/3ds/osystem.h"
 #include "backends/plugins/3ds/3ds-provider.h"
+#ifdef MAUSJAGD_PORT
+#include "backends/platform/3ds/mausjagd.h"
+#endif
 
 #include <3ds.h>
 #include <malloc.h>
@@ -64,6 +67,20 @@ int main(int argc, char *argv[]) {
 	PluginManager::instance().addPluginProvider(new CTRPluginProvider());
 #endif
 
+#ifdef MAUSJAGD_PORT
+	// Standalone build: when started without arguments (Homebrew Launcher, HOME menu),
+	// run the game directly from its fixed folder instead of showing the launcher.
+	// ScummVM creates a temporary target for the game ID and detects the variant in --path.
+	static char autoArg0[] = "mausjagd";
+	static char autoArgPath[] = "--path=" MAUSJAGD_GAME_DIR;
+	static char autoArgGame[] = MAUSJAGD_GAME_ID;
+	static char *autoArgv[] = { autoArg0, autoArgPath, autoArgGame, nullptr };
+	if (argc <= 1) {
+		argc = 3;
+		argv = autoArgv;
+	}
+#endif
+
 	int res = scummvm_main(argc, argv);
 
 	g_system->destroy();
